{
  "comment": "The world of fallen gods (doc/BIOMES_RU.md): where each biome lies, as requirements and not as a drawing. tools/biome_layout.py reads it with a height map and writes the biome map, the ground categories and the control maps. Every biome is a template: on which landmasses it may stand, where on its landmass it wants to be (x, y in the landmass's own box, 0..1, north at y 0), and what ground it wants - each term a curve over a field, 0..1, weighted. The layout takes, at every point, the biome that wants it most, after a seeded wander of the borders, then balances the areas to `share` and checks `borders` (the spec's transitions). `ground` turns a biome into terrain categories (content/config/terrain/categories.json) by the ground inside it; `terrain` is what the biome asks of the terrain generator - read today as control maps, later as the shaping generator's constraints.",
  "fields": {
    "elevation": "height over the landmass's land, 0 at its lowest, 1 at its highest (percentile 99)",
    "slope": "steepness, 0 flat .. 1 at 45 degrees",
    "rugged": "spread of heights within 1.5 km, 0..1",
    "basin": "how much lower than its surroundings (8 km), 0 ridge .. 1 hollow",
    "coast": "distance to the sea, km",
    "lake": "distance to an inland lake, km",
    "x": "west 0 .. east 1 within the landmass box",
    "y": "north 0 .. south 1 within the landmass box"
  },
